# Wave W17-Y (Lake Gallant): gallant elm — a lakefront elm in rich open greens, broad-crowned over the shore road with the highlight lifted clear of the turf, on gallant turf (ground baked in). Lake Gallant’s own tree — split from its cavern-mouth rock rim beside it by softness entire and from Lake Insight’s bank snow pine ahead by season: this elm stands over open water in leaf, that pine over ice in winter.
